# Assurly — UI & design standards

Scoped to UI work rather than always-on, so it costs nothing on backend or scanner changes.

## Visual language

- Clean, minimal, modern: slate/zinc palette, excellent typography, generous white space.
- Avoid typical AI-generated styling — no excessive radial glow, no overused borders, no unpolished colors.
- **The design stays.** Change the engine, rules, and positioning — not the visual design.
  Reuse existing components (e.g. `ShipGatePanel`) for new surfaces instead of inventing new ones.

## Responsiveness

100% responsive on all viewports — mobile, tablet, desktop — in both portrait and landscape.

## Performance

Keep the app fast: `next/image`, local fonts, code splitting, and the other Next.js optimizations.

## Imports

Use absolute path mappings where configured (e.g. `@/components/`) and group imports logically:
external libraries first, then internal.
